      "Turn-flow example: Each player is dealt four cards; four cards are dealt face up to the centre as the pool; the rest form the stock. On your turn, draw one from the stock (when it has cards), then play one card. A normal card captures any available cards of the same rank from the pool or the top set of any opponent's capture pile. A Joker captures all cards of any one rank you choose; an Ace does the same unless the set is protected by a Joker. If you capture, draw again and play again until you play a card that captures nothing; then your turn ends. When the stock is empty, each player plays only one card per turn. The last player to have made a capture takes any remaining table cards. At end of hand, add the point value of your capture pile to your score; first to reach the agreed target (e.g. 500) wins.",
